{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Enable a self-contained, standard rebar MCP HTTP server on the AWS box (which runs Gerrit +\nreview-bot + opcert) so the copilot, codex, and claude clients drive ALL rebar operations through\nit (dogfooding), with setup matching the user-facing docs. Design settled via /rebar-brainstorm and\noperator-approved 2026-08-24 — see the \"OPERATOR-APPROVED DESIGN\" comment for the full rationale and\nthe AWS-cost analysis. Summary of the settled design:\n- Exposure/auth: nginx `/mcp/` TLS edge → loopback-bound `rebar-mcp` HTTP; `static` verifier with\n  per-client bearer PATs. Claude's static-bearer path is verified by rebar's own docs\n  (`docs/mcp-auth.md` §4); Copilot (`~/.copilot/mcp-config.json` `headers`) and Codex\n  (`~/.codex/config.toml` `bearer_token_env_var` / `http_headers`) static-bearer-over-HTTP are\n  verified against those tools' current official docs (research 2026-08-24; citations recorded in the\n  ADR). None of the three requires OAuth.\n- Autodeploy: blue-green immutable-release modeled on the LOCAL `origin/main`-tracking updater\n  (immutable release + atomic nginx-upstream flip + retire-when-idle with retention/cap/alert), NOT\n  the review-bot stop-and-drain — eliminating the bug-7b4a saturation/kill hazard.\n- Certified-op routing: the MCP server signs plan-review + completion op-certs under the box's\n  EXISTING opcert signing environment — env `nava-opcert-prod` (`REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID`), whose pubkey\n  is ALREADY pinned in `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` on `main`. No new env_id. Such a cert\n  VERIFIES against that pinned env; it becomes ENFORCING (not advisory) when\n  `verify.require_environment` is set to that env_id — a single-valued config enablement of the\n  existing gate that PRESERVES ADR 0049's single-env model (NOT the multi-valued behavioral change a\n  distinct MCP env would require). The committed `rebar.toml` does not currently set\n  `verify.require_environment` (so the env-binding check is advisory today, exit 0); flipping it on\n  is a repo-wide toggle owned by the goose slice and called out explicitly, not assumed. Because\n  `verify-opcert` enforces `require_environment` JOINTLY with the grandfather boundary\n  `verify.opcert_enforce_since`, goose sets BOTH together (the boundary at a deploy-time anchor) so\n  only post-deploy closes are enforced and historical closes stay grandfathered/advisory — never\n  retroactively failing the merge-gate; the flip is reversible (unset `require_environment` →\n  advisory everywhere). Code review stays the Gerrit `LLM-Review` vote (no new op-cert kind);\n  opcert/remote-cert coexist.\n\n## Decomposition (8 children; ADR blocks all; dependency-ordered)\n1. deft-evolutive-mosasaur — ADR (exposure/auth + blue-green drain + certified-op routing) + ADR\n   0079 amendment. Blocks all.\n2. cibophobic-holohedral-esok — infra: mcp compose svc + Dockerfile.mcp + nginx `/mcp/` switchable\n   upstream + `/health` in-flight gauge + SIGTERM grace. dep: mosasaur.\n3. panicky-sylphish-foxterrier — autodeploy: mcp blue-green target (build→cutover→retire). deps:\n   mosasaur, esok.\n4. exuberant-blockish-avians — secrets: SSM-materialized per-client bearer PATs + gitignored\n   client-cred template + committed-secret guard. dep: mosasaur.\n5. spoiled-bionic-goose — provision the MCP container to sign under the box's EXISTING opcert env\n   (same SSM key + `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID`; no new env/key); flip enforcement SAFELY by setting\n   `verify.opcert_enforce_since` (deploy-time grandfather boundary) AND `verify.require_environment`\n   together so only post-deploy closes are enforced and historical closes stay advisory; reversible\n   by unset. dep: mosasaur.\n6. unmythical-uninspired-olm — client cfg: copilot/codex/claude static-bearer configs. deps: esok,\n   avians.\n7. inadequate-hydrated-starling — guidance/docs: AGENTS.md MCP-required policy + certified-op\n   wording fix + docs/mcp-auth.md AWS recipe + client guide. deps: mosasaur, spoiled-bionic-goose.\n8. creased-childlike-jackal — approval-gated live 3-client prod verification (operator-performed).\n   dep: olm.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The ADR (deft-evolutive-mosasaur) is landed on `main` deciding exposure/auth + blue-green\n  drain + certified-op routing, with an ADR 0079 amendment. Checked: the ADR file exists on `main`.\n- [ ] The mcp HTTP service + nginx `/mcp/` switchable upstream + `/health` gauge land (esok).\n  Checked: the mcp service boots healthy fail-closed in compose and `/health` returns `in_flight`.\n- [ ] The autodeploy blue-green mcp target lands (foxterrier). Checked: an mcp-only source change\n  triggers a cutover, independent of review-bot/gerrit, without killing an in-flight op.\n- [ ] Per-client bearer PATs are SSM-materialized + gitignored (avians); the MCP container signs\n  under the box's existing opcert env, and `verify.require_environment` + `verify.opcert_enforce_since`\n  are set together (grandfather boundary at a deploy-time anchor) so post-deploy closes are enforced\n  and historical closes stay advisory (spoiled-bionic-goose; no new env); and the three client\n  configs connect (olm). Checked: committed-secret guard test green; a ticket closed after the\n  boundary without a cert FAILs `verify-opcert` while a pre-boundary close is advisory; each client\n  lists the rebar server and runs a basic read tool.\n- [ ] Guidance + docs are updated (starling): AGENTS.md MCP-required policy + certified-op wording\n  correction + docs/mcp-auth.md AWS recipe + client-connection guide. Checked: `grep` shows the new\n  policy and no reference to a nonexistent code-review op-cert.\n- [ ] Live verification (jackal, operator-performed): copilot/codex/claude each execute a basic\n  rebar MCP command against the live endpoint, recorded on the jackal ticket.\n- [ ] Every child ticket is closed. Checked: `rebar list-descendants jira-reb-3527` shows all\n  descendants closed.\n\n## Testing\nTier: **epic integration** — the epic has no standalone test of its own; its oracle is the aggregate\nof its children's gated verification. Each code slice lands `Verified +1` through Gerrit CI carrying\nits own tier-appropriate tests (compose/CLI integration for esok, subprocess/git integration for\nfoxterrier, file/guard tests for avians, signing round-trip for goose, client-connection smoke for\nolm), the ADR/guidance slices verify by inspection, and the operator-run live 3-client smoke (jackal)\nis the end-to-end oracle. The epic closes only when every child is closed on its own evidence and the\nlive verification is recorded."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787605648238175001,"uuid":"5c722d6d-b73b-4254-87e2-b2723675d10f"}